      "Language": "rum",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Respiratory symptoms might originate sometimes in the diseases of another thoracic organ than the lungs, the esophagus, which is able to determine sufferings mimicking pulmonary diseases. The authors review a series of esophageal diseases capable of generating respiratory symptoms, as well as the criteria for differential diagnosis: Zenker diverticulum, esophageal fistula, achalasia, cancer of the esophagus, esophageal cyst and gastro-esophageal reflux disease."},
